1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
YOU PRESS THE GAS, ENGINE REVS UP...

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
BUT THE CAR BARELY SPEEDS UP.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,500
THAT GAP BETWEEN RPM AND SPEED

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,000
IS A CLASSIC SLIPPING CLUTCH SIGN.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
THE CLUTCH DISC LOCKS ENGINE TO GEARBOX.

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,500
WORN FRICTION MATERIAL, OR AN OIL LEAK,

7
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:17,000
MAKES IT SLIDE INSTEAD OF GRIP.

8
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
QUICK CHECK: FLAT ROAD, STEADY SPEED,

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,000
PRESS THE GAS FIRMLY.

10
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,500
RPM JUMPS, CAR DOESN'T RESPOND? THAT'S SLIP.

11
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,000
STOP BY AND WE'LL TAKE A LOOK.
